uot;major_requirement&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Human Biology Requirement\\&quot; is a flexible requirement slot defined by this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a specific course - see the Undergraduate Catalog for the exact eligible options.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&amp;poid=7975&amp;returnto=1177&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag\">Requirement in the major</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Human Biology Requirement</div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"speech-and-hearing-science-ba__box-2-2-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Phonetics&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Basic aspects of articulatory and acoustic phonetics and transcription. Recognize and describe phonetic symbols, transcribe American English using the International Phonetic Alphabet. Describe and explain the normal aspects of speech production, including basics aspects of speech anatomy and physiology, speech acoustics, suprasegmentals, phonological processes, and dialects.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">CDS 286LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Phonetics</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"speech-and-hearing-science-ba__box-2-3-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Perception of Sound&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;This course explores the sense of hearing. It will present the fundamentals of auditory perception, including how sound is produced and is transmitted through the peripheral and central auditory system. We will then delve into the process by which individuals translate the physical properties of sound into their unique perceptual experiences, as well as the methods used to assess those experiences. Linguistic and cognitive contributions to auditory perception will be described. This course will also discuss how sound is useful in everyday life as well as how normal auditory perception differs from that of individuals with hearing loss. Students who are Speech and Hearing Science majors should take this course after they have completed the 200-level courses in the department but before they take the 400-level courses in the department.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">CDS 304LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Perception of Sound</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course\" id=\"speech-and-hearing-science-ba__box-2-4-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;course&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Anatomy and Physiology of the Speech Mechanism&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Involves an anatomic presentation of the neurological, respiratory, laryngeal and supralaryngeal areas of the speech mechanism. Examines neurological, muscular, and skeletal structure for each speech component. Emphasizes in-depth discussion of breathing physiology for speech, laryngeal function for phonation, and supralaryngeal function for articulation and resonance, as well system involvement in swallowing function. Provides an anatomic and physiologic basis for all speech, and voice, and swallowing disorders.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;3&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: null, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: false}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">CDS 388LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Anatomy and Physiology of the Speech Mechanism</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">17 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-spring\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-year\">Year 2</span><span class=\"col-term\">Spring</span></div>\n        <div class=\"col-slots\"><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"speech-and-hearing-science-ba__box-3-0-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div><div class=\"slot\"><div class=\"box box-course box-flexible\" id=\"speech-and-hearing-science-ba__box-3-1-0\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;major_requirement&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;\\&quot;Physical Science Requirement\\&quot; is a flexible requirement slot defined by this major&#x27;s own requirements, not a specific course - see the Undergraduate Catalog for the exact eligible options.&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://catalogs.buffalo.edu/preview_program.php?c